#. {amount} is an amount of money drawn with the coin mark. The chamber is the country's elected assembly.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.ceiling.limit"
msgid "Your office may move up to {amount} at a time; anything larger has to go to the chamber as a bill."
msgstr "Tu cargo puede mover hasta {amount} de una vez; todo lo que pase de eso debe ir a la cámara como proyecto de ley."

#. Said under the Treasury's send form. A ceiling is the largest amount the office may move at one time.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.ceiling.none"
msgid "Your office has no ceiling on this: whatever you enter here is what moves. Anything you would rather the chamber decided has to be taken to it as a bill."
msgstr "Tu cargo no tiene límite en esto: lo que escribas aquí es lo que se mueve. Todo lo que prefieras que decida la cámara debe llevarse a ella como proyecto de ley."

#. Said under the Treasury's send form, to somebody whose office has no spending power on record.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.ceiling.unknown"
msgid "What you send leaves the Treasury immediately."
msgstr "Lo que envíes sale del tesoro público de inmediato."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.aid.send.label"
msgid "Send state aid"
msgstr "Enviar ayuda estatal"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.aid.send.means"
msgid "Give money or goods to another country's Treasury, on the public record, for a stated purpose."
msgstr "Dar dinero o bienes al tesoro público de otro país, de forma pública, con un fin declarado."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.message.send.label"
msgid "Send official messages"
msgstr "Enviar mensajes oficiales"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.message.send.means"
msgid "Send messages to other governments in this country's name. Diplomatic mail is private between the two states."
msgstr "Enviar mensajes a otros gobiernos en nombre de este país. El correo diplomático es privado entre los dos Estados."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.break.label"
msgid "Break treaties"
msgstr "Romper tratados"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.break.means"
msgid "Walk out of an agreement this country signed. It is recorded permanently, and everyone can see who broke what."
msgstr "Salirse de un acuerdo que este país firmó. Queda registrado para siempre, y todos pueden ver quién rompió qué."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.propose.label"
msgid "Propose treaties"
msgstr "Proponer tratados"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.propose.means"
msgid "Offer another country a formal agreement, whether alliance, trade or peace, that binds this one if they accept it."
msgstr "Ofrecer a otro país un acuerdo formal, sea de alianza, comercio o paz, que obliga a este si lo acepta."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.ratify.label"
msgid "Accept treaties"
msgstr "Aceptar tratados"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.diplomacy.treaty.ratify.means"
msgid "Accept a treaty another country has offered, which makes its terms binding on this one."
msgstr "Aceptar un tratado que otro país ha ofrecido, lo que hace que sus condiciones obliguen a este."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.bank.create.label"
msgid "Found a national bank"
msgstr "Fundar un banco nacional"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.bank.create.means"
msgid "Licence a bank to take deposits and lend inside this country."
msgstr "Autorizar a un banco a recibir depósitos y prestar dentro de este país."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.budget.manage.label"
msgid "Set budgets"
msgstr "Fijar presupuestos"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.budget.manage.means"
msgid "Draw up what the state intends to spend and on what. A budget is a public plan, not a payment: the money still moves under a separate authority."
msgstr "Elaborar lo que el Estado piensa gastar y en qué. Un presupuesto es un plan público, no un pago: el dinero se sigue moviendo con una autoridad aparte."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.citizenship.decide.label"
msgid "Admit citizens"
msgstr "Admitir ciudadanos"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.citizenship.decide.means"
msgid "Approve or refuse applications to become a citizen here. Only matters where the country has chosen approval over automatic admission."
msgstr "Aprobar o rechazar solicitudes para ser ciudadano aquí. Solo importa si el país ha elegido la aprobación en lugar de la admisión automática."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.discord.manage.label"
msgid "Link Discord"
msgstr "Vincular Discord"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.discord.manage.means"
msgid "Connect this country to a Discord server for announcements."
msgstr "Conectar este país a un servidor de Discord para los anuncios."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.election.manage.label"
msgid "Call a referendum"
msgstr "Convocar un referendo"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.election.manage.means"
msgid "Ask the whole country a question with two to six answers. The result changes no law by itself. Elections need nobody to call them: every seat goes to its electorate on its own schedule."
msgstr "Hacer una pregunta a todo el país con de dos a seis respuestas. El resultado no cambia ninguna ley por sí solo. Las elecciones no necesitan que nadie las convoque: cada escaño va a su electorado según su propio calendario."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.infrastructure.manage.label"
msgid "Open public works"
msgstr "Abrir obras públicas"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.infrastructure.manage.means"
msgid "Commission transport, industrial or civil works in a province, paid for from the Treasury and the national stockpile. It is what makes a province produce more."
msgstr "Encargar obras de transporte, industriales o civiles en una provincia, pagadas con el tesoro público y la reserva nacional. Es lo que hace que una provincia produzca más."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.law.enact.label"
msgid "Enact laws"
msgstr "Promulgar leyes"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.law.enact.means"
msgid "Sign what the chamber has carried. The world does this on its own within the minute, so it is rarely used by hand."
msgstr "Firmar lo que la cámara ha aprobado. El mundo lo hace solo en menos de un minuto, así que casi nunca se usa a mano."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.law.propose.label"
msgid "Propose bills"
msgstr "Proponer proyectos de ley"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.law.propose.means"
msgid "Put a bill before the chamber for it to vote on."
msgstr "Presentar un proyecto de ley a la cámara para que lo vote."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.law.vote.label"
msgid "Vote on bills"
msgstr "Votar proyectos de ley"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.law.vote.means"
msgid "Cast one of the chamber's votes. A law vote is public and permanent, unlike an election ballot, which is secret."
msgstr "Emitir uno de los votos de la cámara. El voto sobre una ley es público y permanente, a diferencia de la boleta de una elección, que es secreta."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.office.appoint.label"
msgid "Appoint to offices"
msgstr "Nombrar cargos"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.office.appoint.means"
msgid "Put somebody into an office, and form ministries that carry part of your own authority. You cannot grant a power you do not hold."
msgstr "Poner a alguien en un cargo y formar ministerios que llevan parte de tu propia autoridad. No puedes dar un poder que no tienes."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.public_economy.manage.label"
msgid "Run public programmes"
msgstr "Dirigir programas públicos"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.public_economy.manage.means"
msgid "Open and administer subsidies and procurement that citizens and companies apply to, and approve or refuse what they ask for."
msgstr "Abrir y administrar subvenciones y compras públicas a las que se presentan ciudadanos y empresas, y aprobar o rechazar lo que piden."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.research.manage.label"
msgid "Fund research"
msgstr "Financiar investigación"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.research.manage.means"
msgid "Start a tier of national research, which cheapens everything that branch touches for every company in the country, and is the only way to build past level five."
msgstr "Iniciar un nivel de investigación nacional, que abarata todo lo que toca esa rama para todas las empresas del país, y es la única forma de construir más allá del nivel cinco."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.territory.cede.label"
msgid "Give a province back"
msgstr "Devolver una provincia"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.territory.cede.means"
msgid "Hand one of this country's provinces to another country, for good. Nothing but the receiving country's own consent can undo it, which makes it the least reversible thing anybody here can do."
msgstr "Entregar una de las provincias de este país a otro país, para siempre. Nada salvo el consentimiento del propio país receptor puede deshacerlo, lo que lo convierte en lo menos reversible que alguien aquí puede hacer."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.treasury.spend.label"
msgid "Spend from the Treasury"
msgstr "Gastar del tesoro público"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.treasury.spend.means"
msgid "Move public money out of the Treasury, to a citizen, a company or another country. Every movement is on the public ledger with the name of whoever authorised it."
msgstr "Sacar dinero público del tesoro público, hacia un ciudadano, una empresa u otro país. Cada movimiento queda en el registro público con el nombre de quien lo autorizó."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.world_project.contribute.label"
msgid "Give to world projects"
msgstr "Aportar a proyectos del mundo"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.government.world_project.contribute.means"
msgid "Commit this country's money and materials to something the whole world is building. The largest contributors are named when it finishes."
msgstr "Comprometer el dinero y los materiales de este país en algo que construye todo el mundo. Quienes más aportan se nombran al terminar."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.asset.commission.label"
msgid "Build heavy assets"
msgstr "Construir máquinas pesadas"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.asset.commission.means"
msgid "Order the machines a country fights with, such as aircraft, vehicles and heavy weapons, out of the country's own stores and treasury."
msgstr "Encargar las máquinas con las que combate un país, como aviones, vehículos y armas pesadas, con las existencias y el tesoro público del propio país."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.asset.deploy.label"
msgid "Move heavy assets"
msgstr "Mover máquinas pesadas"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.asset.deploy.means"
msgid "Send this country's machines to a province, where they take part in whatever is fought there. They can be lost."
msgstr "Enviar las máquinas de este país a una provincia, donde participan en lo que se combata allí. Se pueden perder."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.battle.launch.label"
msgid "Open battles"
msgstr "Abrir batallas"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.battle.launch.means"
msgid "Start a fight over one province inside a war that is already running. Citizens choose whether to turn up."
msgstr "Iniciar un combate por una provincia dentro de una guerra que ya está en marcha. Los ciudadanos deciden si acuden."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.order.issue.label"
msgid "Issue orders"
msgstr "Dar órdenes"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.order.issue.means"
msgid "Post a military order with a reward, directing this country's fighters at a battle that matters."
msgstr "Publicar una orden militar con recompensa, dirigiendo a los combatientes de este país hacia una batalla importante."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.war.declare.label"
msgid "Declare war"
msgstr "Declarar la guerra"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.war.declare.means"
msgid "Open a war against another country, which lets this country's citizens fight for territory it claims."
msgstr "Abrir una guerra contra otro país, lo que permite a los ciudadanos de este país combatir por el territorio que reclama."

#. A short label on a chip for something an office may do. Keep it brief.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.war.join.label"
msgid "Answer an ally's call"
msgstr "Responder a un aliado"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.military.war.join.means"
msgid "Bring this country into a war an ally is already fighting, on the defending side, where a mutual-defence treaty gives the right. It costs nothing to enter and cannot be taken back: from that moment this country's citizens can fight there, and every other country in that war is at war with this one. Refusing is recorded publicly too."
msgstr "Meter a este país en una guerra que un aliado ya libra, en el bando defensor, donde un tratado de defensa mutua da ese derecho. Entrar no cuesta nada y no se puede deshacer: desde ese momento los ciudadanos de este país pueden combatir allí, y todos los demás países de esa guerra están en guerra con este. Negarse también queda registrado públicamente."

#. Shown for a power of an office that has no explanation written yet.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.noDescription"
msgid "This authority has no description yet. It is real, and the server enforces it."
msgstr "Esta autoridad aún no tiene descripción. Es real, y el servidor la hace cumplir."

#. How an office is filled; a short label on a chip.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.appointment.label"
msgid "Appointed"
msgstr "Nombrado"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.appointment.means"
msgid "Somebody who already holds authority puts a person here, and they hold it at that person's pleasure, until the government that appointed them ends."
msgstr "Alguien que ya tiene autoridad pone aquí a una persona, que lo ocupa a voluntad de quien la nombró, hasta que termine el gobierno que lo hizo."

#. How an office is filled; a short label on a chip.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.directElection.label"
msgid "Elected by the country"
msgstr "Elegido por el país"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.directElection.means"
msgid "Every citizen old enough to vote here chooses who holds it, on a fixed schedule nobody can bring forward except by law."
msgstr "Todo ciudadano con edad para votar aquí elige a quien lo ocupa, en un calendario fijo que nadie puede adelantar salvo por ley."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.fallback.means"
msgid "How this office is filled."
msgstr "Cómo se cubre este cargo."

#. How an office is filled; a short label on a chip.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.indirectElection.label"
msgid "Chosen by the chamber"
msgstr "Elegido por la cámara"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.indirectElection.means"
msgid "The elected chamber picks whoever holds it, and can replace them without going back to the country."
msgstr "La cámara elegida escoge a quien lo ocupa, y puede reemplazarlo sin volver a consultar al país."

#. How an office is filled; a short label on a chip.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.namedSuccession.label"
msgid "Held for life, successor named"
msgstr "De por vida, con sucesor nombrado"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "power.selection.namedSuccession.means"
msgid "It never faces an election. Whoever holds it names a living citizen to follow them, and there is nothing to inherit: Gray Horizon has no families."
msgstr "Nunca se somete a una elección. Quien lo ocupa nombra a un ciudadano vivo para que lo suceda, y no hay nada que heredar: Gray Horizon no tiene familias."

