#. A short description of the game for search results, link previews and an installed app.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.description"
msgid "A nation game on the real Earth: 196 countries, one save file, and every government run by the players in it. In closed alpha."
msgstr "Un juego de naciones en la Tierra real: 196 países, una sola partida guardada y cada gobierno dirigido por los jugadores que hay en él. En alfa cerrada."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.expanded.breaks"
msgid "**Things will break.** That is what this is for. Tell us on Discord."
msgstr "**Habrá cosas que fallen.** Para eso sirve esto. Cuéntanoslo en Discord."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.expanded.deleted"
msgid "**The world will be deleted when the alpha ends.** Every citizen, company, bank, party and government goes with it. We are saying so now rather than afterwards, because finding out afterwards is how a test loses its testers."
msgstr "**El mundo se borrará cuando termine la alfa.** Con él se van todos los ciudadanos, empresas, bancos, partidos y gobiernos. Lo decimos ahora y no después, porque enterarse después es lo que hace que una prueba se quede sin participantes."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.expanded.heading"
msgid "This is a closed alpha, and it is not the real thing yet."
msgstr "Esto es una alfa cerrada, y todavía no es el juego de verdad."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.expanded.waits"
msgid "**Some waits are much shorter than they will be.** Founding a company, changing your name, changing citizenship, calling an election: several of these normally take days or weeks, and have been compressed so that a short test can reach them at all. They are not the real numbers and they will go back up."
msgstr "**Algunas esperas son mucho más cortas de lo que serán.** Fundar una empresa, cambiar de nombre, cambiar de ciudadanía, convocar una elección: varias de estas cosas normalmente tardan días o semanas, y se han comprimido para que una prueba corta pueda llegar a ellas. No son los números reales y volverán a subir."

#. The first of the two lines of the entry card's headline.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.headline.first"
msgid "One world. One citizen."
msgstr "Un mundo. Un ciudadano."

#. The second of the two lines of the entry card's headline.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.headline.second"
msgid "This alpha is deleted when it ends."
msgstr "Esta alfa se borra cuando termina."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.howLong"
msgid "This is a closed alpha, and **the world will be deleted when it ends.** Your citizen, its history and everything it owned go with it. Your account and email address are deleted too, unless you ask us to keep them so you can come back."
msgstr "Esto es una alfa cerrada, y **el mundo se borrará cuando termine.** Tu ciudadano, su historial y todo lo que tenía se van con él. Tu cuenta y tu correo electrónico también se borran, salvo que nos pidas conservarlos para que puedas volver."

#. The name of this stage of the game, on a small badge. Keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.mark"
msgid "Closed alpha"
msgstr "Alfa cerrada"

