#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.privacyDescription"
msgid "What Gray Horizon keeps about you during the closed alpha, where it is kept, how long it is held, and how to have it deleted."
msgstr "Qué guarda Gray Horizon sobre ti durante la alfa cerrada, dónde lo guarda, cuánto tiempo lo conserva y cómo pedir que se borre."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.privacyScope"
msgid "This says what Gray Horizon keeps about you, where it is kept and how to have it deleted. It covers the closed alpha, and it was last updated on 29 September 2026."
msgstr "Aquí se explica qué guarda Gray Horizon sobre ti, dónde lo guarda y cómo pedir que se borre. Cubre la alfa cerrada y se actualizó por última vez el 29 de septiembre de 2026."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.termsDeck"
msgid "These are the plain-language terms of a hobby project, written by the person who runs it rather than by a lawyer. The version above is the one recorded against your account when you registered, and it was last updated on 16 September 2026."
msgstr "Estos son los términos, en lenguaje sencillo, de un proyecto por afición, escritos por quien lo dirige y no por un abogado. La versión de arriba es la que quedó registrada en tu cuenta cuando te registraste, y se actualizó por última vez el 16 de septiembre de 2026."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.termsDeleted.first"
msgid "Every citizen, company, bank, party, government, war and article goes with it. **Nothing you build here is kept.** This is said in the banner inside the game, in the invitation that brought you here, and again now, because finding out afterwards is how a test loses its testers."
msgstr "Con él se van todos los ciudadanos, empresas, bancos, partidos, gobiernos, guerras y artículos. **Nada de lo que construyas aquí se conserva.** Esto se dice en el banner dentro del juego, en la invitación que te trajo aquí y de nuevo ahora, porque enterarse después es lo que hace que una prueba se quede sin participantes."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.termsDeleted.second"
msgid "Some waits are also much shorter than they will be. Founding a company, changing your name, changing citizenship and calling an election normally take days or weeks, and have been compressed so that a short test can reach them at all. Those are not the real numbers."
msgstr "Algunas esperas también son mucho más cortas de lo que serán. Fundar una empresa, cambiar de nombre, cambiar de ciudadanía y convocar una elección normalmente tardan días o semanas, y se han comprimido para que una prueba corta pueda llegar a ellas. No son los números reales."

#. A page description for the Terms, for search results.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.termsDescription"
msgid "What Gray Horizon is, who runs it, that the world is deleted when the closed alpha ends, and how an account is closed."
msgstr "Qué es Gray Horizon, quién lo dirige, que el mundo se borra cuando termina la alfa cerrada y cómo se cierra una cuenta."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.pages.termsWhatThis"
msgid "It is in closed alpha, which means invited testers and a game that is still being built. It is given to you exactly as it is. Nothing here promises that it will be running at any particular moment, or that what you do in it will work. **Things will break.** That is what a test is for, and saying so when they do is the reason you were invited."
msgstr "Está en alfa cerrada, lo que significa participantes invitados y un juego que aún se está construyendo. Se te da tal como es. Nada aquí promete que estará funcionando en un momento concreto, ni que lo que hagas en él vaya a funcionar. **Habrá cosas que fallen.** Para eso sirve una prueba, y avisarnos cuando pase es la razón por la que te invitamos."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.permanence"
msgid "Your citizen lasts until this alpha ends."
msgstr "Tu ciudadano dura hasta que termine esta alfa."

#. The one line of the banner on a phone. Keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.phone"
msgid "Closed alpha: the world will be deleted"
msgstr "Alfa cerrada: el mundo se borrará"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.settingsHeading"
msgid "About this alpha"
msgstr "Sobre esta alfa"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.short"
msgid "The clocks are sped up, and the world will be deleted when this ends. Nothing you build here is kept."
msgstr "Los relojes van acelerados, y el mundo se borrará cuando esto termine. Nada de lo que construyas aquí se conserva."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.termsHeading"
msgid "The world will be deleted when the alpha ends"
msgstr "El mundo se borrará cuando termine la alfa"

#. Said after 'a newspaper in Gray Horizon,' on a printed article: what kind of world this is. Lower case, no full stop.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.closed.worldIs"
msgid "a player-run world in closed alpha"
msgstr "un mundo dirigido por jugadores en alfa cerrada"

#. A short description of the game for search results, link previews and an installed app.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.description"
msgid "A nation game on the real Earth: 196 countries, one save file, and every government run by the players in it. Now in public alpha, open to anybody."
msgstr "Un juego de naciones en la Tierra real: 196 países, una sola partida guardada y cada gobierno dirigido por los jugadores que hay en él. Ahora en alfa pública, abierta a todos."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.expanded.breaks"
msgid "**Things will break.** That is what an alpha is for. Tell us on Discord."
msgstr "**Habrá cosas que fallen.** Para eso sirve una alfa. Cuéntanoslo en Discord."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.expanded.deleted"
msgid "**This world is deleted before the beta opens.** Everything in it goes, the same as the closed alpha did. We are saying so now, before you build anything, and we will give the date at least two weeks ahead."
msgstr "**Este mundo se borra antes de que abra la beta.** Todo lo que hay en él se va, igual que pasó con la alfa cerrada. Lo decimos ahora, antes de que construyas nada, y daremos la fecha con al menos dos semanas de antelación."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.expanded.heading"
msgid "This is the public alpha."
msgstr "Esta es la alfa pública."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.expanded.waits"
msgid "**The waits are the real ones.** Founding a company needs an account a week old, except in a country that is still new: there it needs no waiting, and newcomers vote at once."
msgstr "**Las esperas son las reales.** Fundar una empresa requiere una cuenta con una semana de antigüedad, salvo en un país que aún es nuevo: allí no hay que esperar, y los recién llegados votan de inmediato."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.expanded.why"
msgid "We deleted the closed alpha and started again, open to anybody, so we can see whether the rules and the economy hold up with more people in them."
msgstr "Borramos la alfa cerrada y empezamos de nuevo, abiertos a todos, para ver si las reglas y la economía aguantan con más gente."

#. The first of the two lines of the entry card's headline.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.headline.first"
msgid "One world. One citizen."
msgstr "Un mundo. Un ciudadano."

#. The second of the two lines of the entry card's headline.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.headline.second"
msgid "This alpha is deleted before the beta."
msgstr "Esta alfa se borra antes de la beta."

#. Words between ** and ** are drawn in bold: keep the markers around the matching words.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "stage.public.howLong"
msgid "This world is a public alpha, and **it will be deleted before the beta opens.** Your citizen, its history and everything it owned go with it. Your account and email address are deleted too, unless you ask us to keep them so you can come back. We will say when at least two weeks ahead."
msgstr "Este mundo es una alfa pública, y **se borrará antes de que abra la beta.** Tu ciudadano, su historial y todo lo que tenía se van con él. Tu cuenta y tu correo electrónico también se borran, salvo que nos pidas conservarlos para que puedas volver. Avisaremos de la fecha con al menos dos semanas de antelación."

